<BaseLayout title="About Me | Mark Baldwin-Smith" description="Learn more about the heart and story behind these prayers, poems, and projects.">
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I am a writer, technologist, and minister who believes that creativity and prayer are pathways toward wholeness. My
    work lives at the intersection of faith, storytelling, and digital craftsmanship.
  </p>

  <section class="content">
    <h2>Faith & calling</h2>
    <p>
      I am drawn to spaces where people are seen, heard, and shepherded. Through pastoral leadership, teaching, and
      community care, I aim to steward words that heal and invite transformation.
    </p>

    <h2>Creative practice</h2>
    <p>
      Poetry and prose help me trace the shape of grace in ordinary moments. I write to remember, to lament, to celebrate,
      and to make space for others to do the same. My work is rooted in scripture, the Black church tradition, and the
      rhythms of everyday life.
    </p>

    <h2>Technology & design</h2>
    <p>
      I build thoughtful digital experiences that serve real communities. Whether designing ministry tools, curating
      online spaces, or shaping learning experiences, I bring curiosity, empathy, and strategic clarity to every project.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
</style>
